---
// /thank-you/ — the estimate form's post target.
//
// It existed as four separate pages on the live site and as a dead link in this build: the form
// has always posted to /thank-you/ and the page was never made. One canonical page now; the
// other three 301 here.
//
// NOINDEX IS CORRECT HERE, not a placeholder. A thank-you page ranking in search means people
// land on it without submitting anything, which breaks conversion tracking and reads as a dead
// end to the visitor.
import PageShell from "../layouts/PageShell.astro";
import { MARKET_LIST, NATIONAL } from "../data/markets.js";
---
<PageShell
  badges={false}
  title="Thanks — we'll be in touch | Coldstream Exteriors"
  description="Your request is in. We'll call you back to arrange a free, no-obligation inspection."
  canonical="/thank-you/"
  noindex={true}
  cta={false}
  eyebrow="Request received"
  heading="Thanks — that's all we need for now."
  intro="We'll call you back to arrange a time that suits you. Nothing else is needed from you today."
>
  <section>
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <h2>What happens next</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>
          <strong>We call you back.</strong> Someone from the office nearest you, usually the same
          working day. If you sent this in the evening or over a weekend, it will be the next
          working morning.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>We agree a time.</strong> Most of our areas can be seen within a day or two.
          You do not need to take a day off — for an exterior inspection you usually do not need
          to be home at all, though it is easier if you are.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Someone walks it properly.</strong> On the roof, or along the elevation. Not a
          look from the driveway and not a satellite image. They will photograph what they find.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>You get a written quote.</strong> Scope, materials and the number, in writing.
          Free, no obligation, and yours to keep whatever you decide.
        </li>
      </ol>

      <h2>Nothing is owed and nothing is booked</h2>
      <p>
        There is no deposit for an inspection and no charge for the quote. If the answer turns out
        to be that a repair will do, or that the job can safely wait a season, we will tell you
        that — it is a shorter conversation than the one after a replacement you did not need.
      </p>

      <h2>Two things worth having ready</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Roughly how old the roof or siding is,</strong> if you know. You often will not,
          especially if you did not buy the house new — that is fine, we can usually tell.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Any photos you already took,</strong> particularly of an interior stain or
          something that only shows in heavy rain. They do not replace the inspection, but they
          tell us what to look for.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>If it is a storm or insurance claim</h2>
      <p>
        Say so when we call. We inspect and document the damage the way an adjuster needs it
        documented, and we deal with them directly rather than leaving you to relay messages
        between two parties who both do this for a living. If the roof is open to the weather, we
        cover it first and sort the paperwork second.
      </p>

      <h2>Need us sooner?</h2>
      <p>
        If it is urgent — an active leak, storm damage, something open to the weather — call the
        office for your area directly rather than waiting for the callback.
      </p>
      <ul>
        {MARKET_LIST.map((m) => (
          <li>
            <a href={`/${m.slug}/`}>{m.name}</a> — <a href={m.telHref}>{m.phone}</a>
            <span style="color:var(--cs-steel)"> · {m.office.city}, {m.office.state}</span>
          </li>
        ))}
        <li>Anywhere else — <a href={NATIONAL.telHref}>{NATIONAL.phone}</a></li>
      </ul>

      <h2>While you wait</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="/cincinnati/roofing/roof-repair/">What actually causes most roof leaks</a> — it is rarely the middle of the roof.</li>
        <li><a href="/cincinnati/roofing/insurance-storm-damage/">How a storm claim works</a> — and when filing one is not worth it.</li>
        <li><a href="/cincinnati/siding/james-hardie-siding/">Fiber cement or vinyl</a> — the honest comparison.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
</PageShell>
